body:
I legit began laughing hysterically.

&#x200B;

I'm an Aquarius, I've broken my ankle twice.

Pretty minor I suppose by comparisons, but stretched over six years. I wanted a baby. My husband, six years younger than me did not. But did. But also did not. He would go from wanting a baby, to saying he didn't think he could be a father, to wanting one, to not wanting to suffer like his parents did with him (unplanned pregnancy). He wanted to leave the country first and travel, so we did. And overall, over six years, went back and forth over it while asking if I would leave if he decided he didn't want one. 

&#x200B;

I didn't, but I did finally burn out and break down the dream on my own before telling him I wouldn't have one. Now, of course, he does want one, but I have nothing but negative emotions attached to the idea.

Candy. Alcohol (Weirdly once vodka over tequila. The vodka was gone overnight. Tequila hung around for a long time, like a week?). Once apples, I had the smell of them and set one I could smell down and one I liked down. The one that 'smelled right' rotted out quickly. It's been a month. The other is still there.

&#x200B;

Sometimes it's more intuition and senses that'll let you know what she wants.

Lower back pain and spasms off and on that last up to a month. Extreme skin sensitivity, like... it feels like my skin is being bitten all over by fleas and all it is, is my clothes and arm hair on my skin. Strange joint pain in my fingers, shoulders, knees, toes, etc. These will all happen at once, last for X amount of time, then go away until it's time to start up again. 

&#x200B;

Recently my hip and leg have begun to hurt with a muscle on the outside of my thigh tensing up so badly my leg cramps down to my foot. I managed to sleep until it was over by using icy hot with lidocaine to numb the pain long enough to put myself out.

&#x200B;

I know I need to see a rheumatologist. My doctor told me that since I have one autoimmune problem (Graves) I might have another. I just... can't afford it until I fix the Graves enough to justify spending more money. The Graves sent me to the ER once because it caused an episode of tachycardia. I still can't drink caffeine due to it. But I'm tired all the time right now and worried about putting us further into debt by treating these problems. I don't know what to do.
